 "base_commit": "2e3fe965c963d45ae156c32ef230c7eb7a29a777",
 "issue": 1629,
 "issue_title": "Bug: `ArFrame.__copy__()` shares mutable C++ frame instead of cloning",
 "issue_body": "### What happened?\n\n`copy.copy()` on an `ArFrame` creates a new Python wrapper but still shares the same underlying mutable C++ frame.\n\nCurrent implementation:\n\n```python\n\ndef __copy__(self) -> ArFrame:\n\n    return ArFrame(self._frame, attrs=self._attrs.copy())\n\n```\n\nBecause `self._frame` is reused directly:\n\n- both objects reference the same backend frame\n\n- mutations on one affect the other\n\n- copied objects behave like aliases instead of independent copies\n\n`__deepcopy__()` already correctly uses:\n\n```python\n\nself._frame.clone()\n\n```\n\nbut `__copy__()` does not.\n\n### Area\n\nCSV parser / read_csv / scan_csv\n\n### Minimal reproduction\n\n```python\n\nimport copy\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nimport arnio as ar\n\noriginal = ar.from_pandas(\n\n    pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1, 2, 3]})\n\n)\n\nshallow = copy.copy(original)\n\nar.rename_columns(original, {\"a\": \"b\"})\n\nprint(shallow.columns)\n\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`copy.copy(arframe)` should create an independent `ArFrame`.\n\nExpected:\n\n```python\n\noriginal._frame is shallow._frame\n\n# False\n\n```\n\nMutations to one frame should not affect the other.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n\n\n`copy.copy(arframe)` shares the same mutable backend frame.\n\nCurrent behavior:\n\n```python\n\noriginal._frame is shallow._frame\n\n# True\n\n```\n\nMutations leak across copies silently.\n\n### Impact\n\nBlocks installation or import\n\n### Arnio version\n\n1.18.0\n\n### Install method\n\npip install arnio\n\n### Operating System\n\nmacOS\n\n### Python version\n\n3.12.X\n\n### Environment details\n\n```shell\nStandard `arnio` installation with C++ extension enabled.\n```\n\n### Pre-flight checks\n\n- [x] I searched existing issues and did not find a duplicate.\n- [x] I included a minimal reproduction or explained why one is not possible.\n\n### Additional context\n\nCorrect `__deepcopy__` implementation:\n\n```python\n\ndef __deepcopy__(self, memo: dict) -> ArFrame:\n\n    copied = ArFrame(\n\n        self._frame.clone(),\n\n        attrs={}\n\n    )\n\n```\n\nSuggested fix:\n\n```python\n\ndef __copy__(self) -> ArFrame:\n\n    return ArFrame(\n\n        self._frame.clone(),\n\n        attrs=self._attrs.copy(),\n\n    )\n\n```\n\nThis ensures proper mutation isolation between copied frames.",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1629",
 "pr": 2242,
 "pr_title": "fix: use frame.clone() in ArFrame.__copy__ for mutation isolation",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\n`ArFrame.__copy__()` was reusing `self._frame` directly, causing both the original \r\nand the shallow copy to share the same mutable C++ frame. Mutations on one silently \r\naffected the other. Fixed by calling `self._frame.clone()` \u2014 matching the isolation \r\nguarantee already used by `__deepcopy__()`.\r\n\r\n## Linked issue\r\nFixes #1629\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n- [ ] Feature\r\n- [ ] Performance improvement\r\n- [ ] Documentation\r\n- [x] Tests\r\n- [ ] Refactor\r\n- [ ] CI / packaging\r\n\r\n## Area\r\n- [ ] CSV parser / I/O\r\n- [ ] C++ cleaning engine\r\n- [x] Python API / ArFrame\r\n- [ ] Pipeline / custom steps\r\n- [ ] Data quality / profiling\r\n- [ ] Schema validation\r\n- [ ] pandas interoperability\r\n- [ ] Docs / website\r\n- [ ] Developer tooling\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests -v -k \"copy\"`\r\n35 passed, 2 skipped in 1.47s\r\n\r\n## Screenshots / Media\r\n<img width=\"2940\" height=\"1228\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/532d0fba-fcea-418c-b88c-f792c0d03964\" />\r\n\r\n## Performance Impact\r\nNone \u2014 `clone()` was already used in `__deepcopy__()`. Shallow copy now has \r\nthe same cost as deep copy, which is the correct tradeoff for mutation isolation.\r\n\r\n## GSSoC labels\r\n<!-- For maintainers -->\r\n\r\n## Contributor checklist\r\n- [x] I read the contributing guide.\r\n- [x] I kept the PR focused on one issue or one logical change.\r\n- [x] I added or updated tests for behavior changes.\r\n- [ ] I added or updated docs/examples for public API changes.\r\n- [x] I checked that generated files, logs, and local build artifacts are not committed.\r\n- [x] My PR title uses Conventional Commits (`fix:`).\r\n\r\n## Maintainer notes\r\nThe existing `test_arframe_shallow_copy` was asserting the buggy behavior \r\n(`copied._frame is frame._frame`). Updated it to assert the correct behavior. \r\nAdded `test_shallow_copy_independent_frame` as explicit regression coverage \r\nper the issue spec.",
